  "comparison_readings": {
    "middle_perfect": "The lexical e survives in cikleśe, whereas the weakened radical in the divādi perfect gives cikliśe. Maitreya directly contrasts them in separate entries.",
    "class_nine_aorist": "When the ū-marked root omits iṭ, a ś-final root with i as upadhā meets 3.1.45 and takes ksa. With iṭ, sic remains and gives the independent sigmatic aorist. The alternative affects each of the nine persons and numbers.",
    "class_four_aorist": "The actual archive for this root has the same nine seṭ sigmatic words as class one. A different third singular akliṣṭa is directly in the printed Mādhavīya and in the XML. No complete no-iṭ series for this reading has been inferred.",
    "active_perfect_2sg": "The archive gives cikleśitha/cikleṣṭha. Mādhava prints cikliśitha/cikleṣṭha, sharing the second and differing in the radical vowel of the first. The short-vowel word has an explicit alternate witness, without counting a second cell."
